course: dictionary
lesson: 5554
title: Precise words paint pictures
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lemony is a describing word. It tells you what something tastes like, what it smells like, or what colour it is. «We baked a lemony cake for the party.» The word lemony tells the reader the cake tastes of lemon, so they can almost taste it.
explain: One precise word paints a picture. «It was a nice cake» tells us very little, but «a lemony cake» tells us exactly what it is like. When you write, look for the describing word that gives the most detail.
explain: Lemony can also describe colour. «The walls were painted a lemony yellow.» Here it means the pale yellow of a lemon peel. A word like lemony helps readers see, smell or taste what you mean.
fact: Lemony is an adjective, a describing word.
fact: Lemony means tasting or smelling of lemon.
fact: Lemony can also mean the pale yellow colour of a lemon.
fact: «A lemony cake» tells the reader about taste, «a lemony smell» tells them about smell, and «lemony yellow» tells them about colour.
fact: One precise word, like «lemony», paints a picture, while piling up «big, huge, enormous, massive» just makes the reader wait.
exercise: «We ate a lemony cake after lunch.» What does lemony mean here? | Made of wood | Loud and noisy | Very large | *Tasting of lemon
exercise: «The walls were painted a lemony yellow.» What colour is this? | *Pale yellow, like a lemon | Dark green, like a forest | Bright red, like a fire engine | Black, as dark as night
exercise: Which word tells the reader the most about the taste of the cake? "The cake was ___." | good | big | nice | *lemony
test: «The kitchen filled with a lemony smell.» What does lemony tell the reader? | *What the air smelled like | How big the kitchen was | What time of day it was | How many people were cooking
test: Which word paints the clearest picture of a jumper? "It was a ___ jumper." | *lemony yellow | good | nice | big
exam: Which word best describes a drink that tastes of lemon? | big | nice | *lemony | loud
